  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Monday)\nIssued at 1210 AM CDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge will be centered over Tennessee into the \nCarolinas Wednesday into Friday. The remnants of tropical system \nEdoard is forecast to drift north-northwest over portions of the \neastern half of Texas on Wednesday. Our area can expect hot and dry \nconditions Wednesday with highs in the mid/upper 90s in our southern \ncounties, and upper 90s to 102 across the northern half of our area. \n\nWith a slight increase in moisture Thursday and Friday, our eastern \nand southeastern counties (generally east of a Brownwood to Junction \nline) will have a slight chance (15-25 percent) of showers and \nthunderstorms. Highs Thursday will be similar to Wednesday. With a \nslight weakening of the 850mb thermal ridge Friday along with a \nslight increase in cloud cover, highs should back off a few degrees \nFriday.  \n\nThe aforementioned upper ridge is progged to shift back to the west \nand north over portions of the Midwest and Great Plains during the \nweekend. This is expected to keep our temperatures above normal and \nkeep any rain chances minimal Saturday into Monday. Daily highs \nshould be mostly in the mid 90s in our southern counties, mid and \nupper 90s in our central counties, and upper 90s to 101 across the \nBig Country.",
